          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Occupational therapy suits people who want to help others regain the daily activities that matter to them, such as dressing, writing, working or playing, and it is a good career only if you can handle patient-facing clinical work, slow progress and the registration rules that apply."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "It is a regulated allied health career built on helping people function in daily life."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Course recognition, registration and scope of practice differ by state and council."
          }
        ]
      },
